From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller: drop the policy binding before the reload frees it

Every config reload leaves some nodes pointing at freed memory, and the
tripwire built to catch exactly that cannot see it.

cntlr_config_reload() moves the current lists aside, parses fresh ones out of
UCI, and ends with clean_agent_policies(&old) - which frees every
struct node_policy that the nodes in agentlist are holding in n->np.
cntlr_resync_config() then re-binds them, but it walks the NEW config
nodelist:

	list_for_each_entry(np, &c->cfg.nodelist, list)
		n = cntlr_find_node(c, np->agent_id);
		if (n) n->np = np;

so it only reaches nodes that still have a section. A node whose UCI section
was removed, and a node that never had one - the case the invariant check
itself names - is never visited, and keeps a pointer into freed memory for as
long as it lives.

The check at the agent-policy send site tests !n->np. A dangling pointer is
not NULL, so it passes, is dereferenced, and nodes_without_policy - the
counter that exists to make this visible - stays 0 while it happens. The
tripwire is silent precisely in the case it was built for.

Clearing the bindings before the reload costs one pass over agentlist and
converts a use-after-free into the condition the code already reports. It
also makes nodes_without_policy mean what its comment says.

This needs no SIGHUP: cntlr_resync_config() runs on the ordinary config-check
path, so an unbound node is reached by ordinary operation.

Verify: remove a `node` section for a live agent from mapcontroller and
reload. `ubus call map.controller status` must show nodes_without_policy
counting up instead of the controller reading freed memory.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/cntlr.c
+++ b/src/cntlr.c
@@ -1740,6 +1740,28 @@
 {
 	uint32_t diff;
 	struct node_policy *np = NULL;
+	struct node *node = NULL;
+
+	/* Let go before the ground moves.
+	 *
+	 * cntlr_config_reload() moves the current lists aside, parses fresh
+	 * ones from UCI and then frees the old with clean_agent_policies().
+	 * Every node in agentlist is holding a pointer into what it just
+	 * freed. The loop below re-binds them - but it walks the NEW config
+	 * nodelist, so it only reaches nodes that still have a section. A
+	 * node whose section was removed, or one that never had one, is
+	 * never visited and keeps pointing at freed memory.
+	 *
+	 * The invariant check at the agent-policy send site tests !n->np. A
+	 * freed pointer is not NULL, so it walks straight past the tripwire
+	 * and is dereferenced - and nodes_without_policy, the counter that
+	 * exists to make exactly this visible, stays at 0 while it happens.
+	 *
+	 * Clearing first costs one pass and turns a use-after-free into the
+	 * condition the code already knows how to report.
+	 */
+	list_for_each_entry(node, &c->agentlist, list)
+		node->np = NULL;
 
 	diff = cntlr_config_reload(&c->cfg);
 
